ANTI_CONCENTRATION
For sigma<=1, conditional Gaussian means are separated by >=sqrt(2).
Any interval of radius 1/2 has length 1<sqrt(2), hence contains at most one conditional mean.
The component whose mean is outside the interval contributes <=1/2 conditionally; the other <=1.
Thus Q_xi(1/2)<= (1/2)*1 + (1/2)*(1/2) = 3/4.

